{"text": "Melvin S. Tennyson\n\u2018St Augustine, Florida\n\nE-Mail:\n\nSUMMARY\n\nHighly decorated and accomplished executive management professional with extensive background in Patrol,\nInvestigations, Special Operations, Training, Community Relations, Executive Administration, and Staff/Leadership\nDevelopment.\n\n27 years of experience in law enforcement, with comprehensive skills in developing policies and procedures,\nadministering budgets, program development and implementing new programs.\n\nProven expertise in executive level leadership, policy and procedure development, and community relations programs.\nRecognized for a keen understanding of how to organize and deploy resources. Highly proficient in dealing with multi-\nfunctional resources and crisis management.\n\nAdept at liaising with foreign, Federal, State and Local govemment agencies, community groups, and general public. A\n\nconsistent record of accomplishments as an executive manager, with outstanding leadership, organizational, and\n\u2018communication skills.\n\nExperience\n\nOkaloosa County Airports Police (Eglin AFB) February 2012- Present.\n\nChief of Police:\n\u2018+ Stood up Police Department as first Chief of Police located on Eglin Air Force Base.\n\n\u2018+ Develop plans and procedures designed to safeguard employees, visitors, citizens and property\nagainst criminal activity, civil disorder, terrorism and other threats.\n\u2018+ Represent agency in meetings, in the media, and public events. Acts as a spokesperson and is a\nvisible leader within the organization promoting open communication and effectively articulating\nexpectations.\n\u2018+ Prepares, justifies, and administers the program budget. Oversees procurement and\ncontracting to achieve desired results. Monitors expenditures and uses cost-benefit thinking\nto set priorities.\n\u2018+ Established policies, professional standards, and training requirements that guide the management of\nall police personnel. Implements measure to strengthen and empower the police chain of command in\na way that encourages accountability across all levels.\n\u2018+ Collaborates with other agencies and organizations to ensure integrated use of police resources.\nProvides senior level guidance to ensure consistent and appropriate actions of police personnel\n\u2018+ Directs interagency coordination within the intelligence community, homeland security, military, and\nfederal, state, and/or local law enforcement agencies.\n\u2018+ Over all command of police agency in a national, intemational and multi-cultural environment.",
